    "reason": "The assertion conflates a standard architectural mechanism (self-attention aggregating values) with an absolute guarantee for all implementations. While self-attention *can* produce context-aware representations via value aggregation, this is not guaranteed if the attention weights are zeroed out (e.g., in masked regions or specific pruning scenarios), if the model uses linear projections that dec","counterexample": "A transformer layer where the attention mask forces all attention weights to zero for a specific token (common in causal masking for autoregressive generation) results in that token's representation being derived solely from its value vector and positional embedding, not an aggregation of *all* tokens' values. Thus, the 'aggregation from all tokens' condition fails.",
